/devil#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e6103ceb0d0ca584ab","definition":"A dust devil.","example":"The formation of tornados and water-spouts is very probably identical with that of dust-storms and \"devils,\" viz., a sudden disturbance of the vertical equilibrium of the atmosphere, where by an upward rush of air is generated, which rapidly becomes spiral.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["diabolo","diablo"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devil#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6d09381154cac1965c","definition":"A barren, unproductive and unused area.","example":"devil strip","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dialectal, in-compounds","register":"dialectal, in-compounds","wordFamily":["diabolo","diablo"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devil#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a629bc041466c43a5f","definition":"A dish, as a bone with the meat, broiled and excessively peppered; a grill with Cayenne pepper.","example":"Men and women busy in baking, broiling, roasting oysters, and preparing devils on the gridiron.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["diabolo","diablo"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devil#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7d1c0f578403a6c4c5","definition":"A machine for tearing or cutting rags, cotton, etc., as used in the production of mungo or shoddy.","example":"The woollen things are torn to pieces by a machine having spiked rollers (termed a devil), cleansed, and the fibre spun with a certain proportion of new wool, the yarn being afterwards woven into the full-bodied but flimsy fabric termed shoddy.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["diabolo","diablo"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devil#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:75364f4f286264f7a1","definition":"A Tasmanian devil.","example":"He removes his food, water, and torch from the pack and then pushes it to the far end of the tent – no devil is going to rip his pack apart tonight.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["diabolo","diablo"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devil#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8ce87268583603277a","definition":"An endurance event where riders who fall behind are periodically eliminated.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"slang","register":"slang","wordFamily":["diabolo","diablo"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devil#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:719aed9eadfb962780","definition":"Ellipsis of devil seam (“the seam between garboard strake and the keel, on wooden boats”).","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"abbreviation, alt-of, ellipsis","register":"abbreviation, alt-of, ellipsis","wordFamily":["diabolo","diablo"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devil#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:167149d87e5d2f5085","definition":"To make like a devil; to invest with the character of a devil.","example":"","pos":"verb","syno